    "metadata": {
      "title": "A short proof of Ball's plank theorem",
      "authors": [
        "Arseniy Akopyan",
        "Alexander Polyanskii"
      ],
      "abstract": "We give a short proof of the following theorem of K. Ball: If a centrally symmetric convex body $K\\subset \\mathbb R^d$ is covered by finitely many planks, then the sum of their relative widths with respect to $K$ is at least $1$.",
